- op: discuss  # 020c
  at: '2026-11-18T00:06:10Z'  # 020c
  by: agent  # 020c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 020c
  clock: 4  # 020c
  nonce: 020c  # 020c
  message: "Fixed in PR #2242 (dev fc2d2d8a9). import_closure.build takes the functions the index saw run under no test's context (selection_index.functions_run_at_import) and counts an import inside one as an import of the file; coverage-select import-closure passes them. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the item's own repro re-run on the live index (2026-11-18 00:05 UTC; output in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/bar/import_time_functions.txt): the same one-statement edit to io_boundary.load_catalog, real 'coverage-select import-closure' -> exit 0, '1 file(s) with changed import-time code are loaded by 583 test file(s)', and all 9 test_haskell*.py / test_jupyter*.py files are in the answer (3 before; the 6 named in the description were in neither answer). In the selection bed, a new module (derives_at_import.py: imports limits inside _derive() and calls _derive() as it loads) has its test in the manifest for a change to the constant, where the slice misses it; with the marks not passed to the graph the bed test fails. 12 mutations red. MEASURED COST on this tree (lazyimport/closure_sizes.txt, computed before the merge with 153 marks): 19 import edges added in 10 files; mean closure over 372 source files 206.5 -> 229.8 test files, median 16 -> 18, 21 closures grew. NOT CLOSED BY THIS: (1) the graph WALK still does not reach those 6 files; the closure adds them, and the closure fires only for a change to import-time code (a module or class body, or a marked function). A change to an UNMARKED function of io_boundary.py that a marked function calls at import is not such a change and is selected by the walk and the coverage record alone. I have not checked whether that shape loses a test. (2) An import inside a function that does not run at import is still not followed (the bed's known miss, test_reads_lazily). (3) A function that newly starts to run at import is unmarked until a folded run sees it."  # 020c
- op: discuss  # c7ab
  at: '2026-11-18T00:06:19Z'  # c7ab
  by: agent  # c7ab
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c7ab
  clock: 5  # c7ab
  nonce: c7ab  # c7ab
  message: "CORRECTION to point (1) of my closing note. I wrote that a change to an UNMARKED function which a marked function calls at import is selected by the walk and the coverage record alone, and that I had not checked whether that loses a test. That shape cannot occur as described: a function that executes during an import has its statements run under no test's context, so the fold marks IT too (the mark is per function that ran, not per function called from a module body). io_boundary.load_catalog is itself marked for exactly that reason. What remains true in (1): the graph walk does not reach the six files, and the import closure is what adds them. Points (2) and (3) stand."  # c7ab
